// ScyllaDB's REST management API, recorded comprehensively: one of the
// "comprehensive" suites of servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers
// (the README's "Pattern for comprehensive suites" says what they share;
// couchdb/test_couchdb.ae is the reference implementation).
//
// What is recorded: the HTTP/JSON API on port 10000 that nodetool, the
// monitoring tools and the Scylla Manager agent talk to (storage_service,
// system, column_family, failure_detector, gossiper, cache_service, ...),
// from `scylladb/scylla:6.2` (6.2.3). Not the CQL port (9042, a binary
// protocol), Alternator (8000, DynamoDB's API, a different suite's job) or
// the Prometheus port (9180, a flood of counters).
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes
// are the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test
// framework that makes the same requests, in the same order, against a
// Servirtium replay server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things.
// Any Servirtium implementation replays them. Every request is plain
// HTTP/1.1 with one header and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
// (the POSTs and DELETEs have no body and no Content-Type). Playback is
// strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as written in
// this file) and the recorded request headers, and fails a case whose
// recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and Content-Length
// are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
//
// PORTING, the tape for each case: <case>.md beside this file, where <case>
// is the second argument of servirtium.recording(...) in that case. The
// cases are independent: each makes the keyspace it needs (a fixed name,
// with one table `items` and two rows) BEFORE the recording starts and drops
// it after, both through `cqlsh` inside the container, so none of it is on a
// tape. A tape starts from "the keyspace exists", and any one replays alone
// and in any order. Where a case changes the schema or the data between two
// requests (schema_version_changes_with_a_ddl_statement, flushes_and_
// compacts_a_keyspace) that step is a cqlsh call between two requests; it is
// not on the tape, so on replay just skip it: the second request's answer is
// already there.
//
// Authentication: none. The REST API is unauthenticated (it listens on
// loopback inside the container by default; the module's rest_api() option
// makes it listen on 0.0.0.0 so the published port reaches it), so there is
// no login tape and no credential on any tape.
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them and the
// interactions each touched ("none" where it did not). In short:
//   - normalized (each distinct value a stable {{name-N}} token, the same
//     token wherever it recurs, because a client sends it back): UUIDs
//     ({{uuid-N}}: the host id, the schema version, a raft leader's id) and
//     the node's IPv4 address ({{ip-N}}: the container's address on the
//     engine's network, different on every machine and run).
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): the node's tokens
//     (256 random numbers per run, so the whole array becomes one
//     "TOKEN" entry), the generation number (the node's start time in Unix
//     seconds), bytes loaded, a snapshot's byte sizes, the uptime in
//     milliseconds.
//   - redacted: nothing; there are no credentials.
//   - left out: nothing beyond the Date response header, as everywhere.
// Leave alone, because they are the same every run: the release versions
// (3.0.8 is the Cassandra version Scylla claims to be, the Scylla version is
// 6.2.3-0.20250119.bff9ddde1283), the datacenter and rack names, the
// partitioner, the RPC timeouts, the log levels.
//
// PORTING: in playback, a normalized value comes back as its token,
// verbatim: the host id is "{{uuid-1}}", the node address "{{ip-1}}". Treat
// every id and address as an opaque string (never assert its length or
// shape) and send it back exactly as received. The Seastar HTTP server sends
// `Content-Length` and `Content-Type: application/json` on JSON (and no
// Content-Type on the empty 200 of a POST); every body here is JSON or a
// bare JSON scalar ("info", 0.25, true).
//
// Order that is not deterministic
// -------------------------------
// Seastar builds several listings from hash maps, so their order depends on
// what was inserted and when: /column_family/ (every table), /column_family/
// name, /column_family/name/keyspace, /storage_service/keyspaces (also
// ?type=non_local_strategy), /storage_service/logging_level and
// /system/logger (a few hundred names). The tapes have each of these arrays
// sorted (Servirtium's stable order, scoped to those requests: by each
// element's canonical JSON, so names alphabetically), and replay serves that
// order; live, a client must not rely on any order, and the cases do not.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: build and cluster identity (release_version, scylla_release_version,
// cluster_name, partitioner_name, snitch), the node's identity and ring
// state (host_id, tokens, tokens_endpoint, ownership, operation_mode,
// is_initialized, gossiping, native_transport, nodes/joining|leaving|moving,
// load_map, raft/leader_host), keyspaces (all, user, non_local_strategy,
// natural_endpoints, ownership per keyspace), table metrics, flush and
// compaction, snapshots (take, list, delete), the schema version before and
// after a DDL statement, log levels (get, set, reset, the 400s), tracing
// probability and slow-query settings, gossip and the failure detector,
// storage_proxy timeouts and hinted handoff, the compaction and task
// managers, the cache service, node paths, uptime, the swagger index, and
// the representative errors (400 unknown keyspace, level, logger and
// missing parameter; 404; 500 "not supported yet").
// Out: describe_ring (256 ranges of random tokens), /failure_detector/
// endpoints (gossip application states with tokens, generation and
// timestamps), /compaction_manager/compaction_history (ids and times),
// /messaging_service/messages/* (counters that move with every request),
// repair, streaming and decommission/removenode (multi-node, asynchronous),
// the Prometheus endpoint, and anything that stops or reconfigures the node
// (drain, decommission, truncate).
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test scylladb/test_scylladb.ae                    container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test scylladb/test_scylladb.ae  write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test scylladb/test_scylladb.ae  fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test scylladb/test_scylladb.ae  no container: the tapes
// The cases share one container (started on the first one, removed at the
// end). ScyllaDB is slow to start (about a minute): the module waits for CQL
// and for the REST port, then the test polls /storage_service/operation_mode
// until it says NORMAL before the first case, outside any recording.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.http.client
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.scylladb

const IMAGE = "scylladb/scylla:6.2"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would; Aether's std.http.client adds none. Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var api: string = ""
var last_content_type: string = ""

// One request with no body: (status, body, error).
fn http_send(method: string, url: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    last_content_type = client.response_header(r, "Content-Type")
    client.response_free(r)
    // JSON without the whitespace between tokens (servirtium.json_compact), so
    // the assertions hold live and against a pretty-printed tape alike.
    return st, servirtium.json_compact(b), ""
}

// A request to the current recording's base URL: (status, body). A transport
// error fails the case.
fn rest(method: string, path: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// GET path, expect 200 and exactly this body.
fn expect_body(path: string, want: string) {
    st, b = rest("GET", path)
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET ${path}: ${b}")
    spec.assert_str_eq(b, want, "GET ${path}")
}

// GET path, expect 200 and a body containing this.
fn expect_contains(path: string, want: string) {
    st, b = rest("GET", path)
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "GET ${path}: ${b}")
    spec.assert_contains(b, want, "GET ${path}: ${b}")
}

// A request that must fail with this status and a message containing want.
fn expect_error(method: string, path: string, status: int, want: string) {
    st, b = rest(method, path)
    spec.assert_eq(st, status, "${method} ${path}: ${b}")
    spec.assert_contains(b, want, "${method} ${path}: ${b}")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live container the cases share (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var shared_addr: string = ""
var shared_container: ptr = null

// Run a CQL statement inside the container with cqlsh (live only; never on
// a tape).
fn cql(stmt: string) {
    if servirtium.live() != 1 { return }
    code, out, err = tc.exec(shared_container as *docker.Container, ["cqlsh", "-e", stmt])
    spec.assert_eq(code, 0, "cqlsh: ${stmt}: ${out} ${err}")
}

// The REST API's base URL, starting the container on first use ("" on
// failure). Waits until the node says NORMAL (CQL being up is not enough:
// the API answers 200 for most things earlier).
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_addr) > 0 { return shared_addr }
    c, err = scylladb.run(IMAGE) { rest_api() }
    if c == null {
        spec.fail("scylladb starts: ${err}")
        return ""
    }
    shared_container = c as ptr
    spec.assert_ok(err, "scylladb starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    host, herr = scylladb.rest_api_connection_host(c)
    spec.assert_ok(herr, "REST API host")
    base = "http://${host}"
    tries = 0
    ready = 0
    while ready == 0 && tries < 120 {
        st, b, rerr = http_send("GET", "${base}/storage_service/operation_mode")
        if rerr == "" && st == 200 && string.contains(b, "NORMAL") == 1 { ready = 1 }
        if ready == 0 { sleep(1000) }
        tries = tries + 1
    }
    spec.assert_eq(ready, 1, "the node reaches NORMAL")
    if ready == 0 { return "" }
    shared_addr = base
    return shared_addr
}

// A keyspace the case works in: one node, vnodes (tablets off, so ownership
// and natural_endpoints work; a tablet keyspace answers 400 there), one
// table `items` (id int primary key, name text) and two rows.
fn make_keyspace(ks: string) {
    cql("DROP KEYSPACE IF EXISTS ${ks}")
    cql("CREATE KEYSPACE ${ks} WITH replication = {'class': 'NetworkTopologyStrategy', 'datacenter1': 1} AND tablets = {'enabled': false}")
    cql("CREATE TABLE ${ks}.items (id int PRIMARY KEY, name text)")
    cql("INSERT INTO ${ks}.items (id, name) VALUES (1, 'a')")
    cql("INSERT INTO ${ks}.items (id, name) VALUES (2, 'b')")
}

// Start a case: in a live mode the shared container and, when the case uses
// a keyspace, that keyspace (none of it recorded); then the recording. Sets
// `api`; returns the recording handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string, ks: string) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        // DROP KEYSPACE takes a "pre-drop-<time>" snapshot of every table
        // (auto_snapshot), so an earlier case's cleanup leaves some behind:
        // delete every snapshot (no tag means all) before this case starts.
        http_send("DELETE", "${addr}/storage_service/snapshots")
        if string.length(ks) > 0 { make_keyspace(ks) }
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("scylladb", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// End a case: the recording, then (live) the case's keyspace dropped.
fn finish(rec: ptr, ks: string) {
    servirtium.end_recording(rec)
    if string.length(ks) > 0 { cql("DROP KEYSPACE IF EXISTS ${ks}") }
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // The node's tokens: 256 random numbers per run (vnodes), as a JSON array
    // of strings (/storage_service/tokens) and as {"key": token, "value":
    // address} objects (/tokens_endpoint). Nobody sends them back; the whole
    // array becomes one entry. These two come first so that the address
    // inside the second is swallowed, not normalized.
    servirtium.collapse("\\[\"-?[0-9]{10,}\"(, \"-?[0-9]{10,}\")*\\]", "[\"TOKEN\"]")
    servirtium.collapse("\\[\\{\"key\":\"-?[0-9]{10,}\",\"value\":\"[^\"]*\"\\}(, \\{\"key\":\"-?[0-9]{10,}\",\"value\":\"[^\"]*\"\\})*\\]", "[{\"key\":\"TOKEN\",\"value\":\"ADDRESS\"}]")
    // The host id, the schema version (a time UUID that changes with every
    // DDL statement), a snapshot's or task's id: UUIDs, different every run.
    // Normalized, since a client reads one and sends it back (nodetool does
    // with the host id) or compares two (before and after a DDL statement).
    servirtium.normalize(servirtium.UUID, "uuid")
    // The node's address: the container's IP on the engine's network. It
    // appears as a map key and a value all over (host_id, ownership,
    // gossiper, load_map, natural_endpoints), and a client sends it back
    // (/failure_detector/endpoints/..., /messaging_service/version?addr=).
    // Four dotted numbers, not preceded or followed by a digit or dot, so a
    // three-part version (3.0.8) and the 6.2.3-0.2025... build string are
    // left alone; 127.x (the recorder's own, already {{request.host}}) too.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<![0-9.])(?!127\\.)[0-9]{1,3}(\\.[0-9]{1,3}){3}(?![0-9.])", "ip")
    // The generation number: the node's start time in Unix seconds, a bare
    // ten-digit number (the lookarounds keep it off the 19-digit tokens).
    servirtium.collapse("(?<![0-9])1[0-9]{9}(?![0-9])", "1000000000")
    // /storage_service/load_map: bytes on disk per node, a number that moves
    // as the node writes. The only place `"value": <digits>}` occurs.
    servirtium.collapse("\"value\": [0-9]+\\}", "\"value\": 0}")
    // /storage_service/ownership: the share of the ring as a string
    // ("1", "0.9999998", "1.0000004"): the 256 random tokens' rounding differs
    // every run. Collapsed to "1".
    servirtium.collapse("\"value\": \"[01](\\.[0-9]+)?\"", "\"value\": \"1\"")
    // A snapshot's size on disk and its live part (block-size dependent).
    servirtium.collapse("\"total\":[0-9]+,\"live\":[0-9]+", "\"total\":0,\"live\":0")
    // /system/uptime_ms: a bare number of milliseconds (three to nine digits:
    // from a fraction of a second to a day or so) that is the whole body. The
    // rules run over each field, so (?m) anchors the line: a line of nothing
    // but digits is a bare body. Only that call returns such a body (the other
    // bare numbers on the tapes are one or two digits, and the ten-digit
    // generation number is the rule above).
    servirtium.collapse("(?m)^[0-9]{3,9}$", "1000000")
    // The listings Seastar builds from hash maps (see "Order that is not
    // deterministic" above): each root array sorted, for those requests only.
    servirtium.sort_json_array_at("^/(column_family/(name(/keyspace)?)?|storage_service/keyspaces|storage_service/logging_level|system/logger)(\\?|$)", "", "")
    // Sorted JSON is only written pretty-printed (a sort rule without
    // pretty_json is refused): every JSON response body on these tapes is
    // indented, so a reader sees it was rewritten.
    servirtium.pretty_json(2)
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "ScyllaDB REST API") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/release_version, /scylla_release_version,
        // /cluster_name, /partitioner_name, then GET /snitch/name, /snitch/datacenter,
        // /snitch/rack and GET /system/highest_supported_sstable_version. Each
        // answers 200 with a bare JSON string.
        spec.it("reports the release and the cluster identity") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_release_and_the_cluster_identity", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/storage_service/release_version", "\"3.0.8\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/scylla_release_version", "\"6.2.")
            expect_body("/storage_service/cluster_name", "\"Test Cluster\"")
            expect_body("/storage_service/partitioner_name", "\"org.apache.cassandra.dht.Murmur3Partitioner\"")
            expect_body("/snitch/name", "\"org.apache.cassandra.locator.SimpleSnitch\"")
            expect_body("/snitch/datacenter", "\"datacenter1\"")
            expect_body("/snitch/rack", "\"rack1\"")
            expect_body("/system/highest_supported_sstable_version", "\"me\"")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/host_id (a list of {key: address,
        // value: host id}), /storage_service/hostid/local (the id as a string),
        // /storage_service/tokens (array of strings), /tokens_endpoint,
        // /ownership (the share of the ring, "1" for the only node, collapsed), /generation_number, /operation_mode, /is_initialized,
        // /is_starting, /gossiping, /native_transport, /rpc_server (false: the
        // Thrift server is gone), /join_ring, /nodes/joining, /nodes/leaving,
        // /nodes/moving, /load_map, /removal_status and GET /raft/leader_host.
        // The host id returned by hostid/local is the one in host_id's value,
        // and raft/leader_host names the same node: all {{uuid-1}} on replay.
        spec.it("reports the node identity and the state of the ring") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_node_identity_and_the_state_of_the_ring", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = rest("GET", "/storage_service/host_id")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "host_id: ${b}")
            // one node: [{"key": "<address>", "value": "<host id>"}]
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key\":\"", "an address")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"", "a host id")
            st2, local = rest("GET", "/storage_service/hostid/local")
            spec.assert_eq(st2, 200, "hostid/local")
            spec.assert_contains(b, string.substring(local, 1, string.length(local) - 1), "hostid/local is host_id's value")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/tokens", "[\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/tokens_endpoint", "[{\"key\":\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/ownership", "\"value\":\"")
            st3, gen = rest("GET", "/storage_service/generation_number")
            spec.assert_eq(st3, 200, "generation_number: ${gen}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/operation_mode", "\"NORMAL\"")
            expect_body("/storage_service/is_initialized", "true")
            expect_body("/storage_service/is_starting", "false")
            expect_body("/storage_service/gossiping", "true")
            expect_body("/storage_service/native_transport", "true")
            expect_body("/storage_service/rpc_server", "false")
            expect_body("/storage_service/join_ring", "true")
            expect_body("/storage_service/nodes/joining", "[]")
            expect_body("/storage_service/nodes/leaving", "[]")
            expect_body("/storage_service/nodes/moving", "[]")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/load_map", "\"value\":")
            expect_body("/storage_service/removal_status", "\"No token removals in process.\"")
            st4, leader = rest("GET", "/raft/leader_host")
            spec.assert_eq(st4, 200, "raft/leader_host: ${leader}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(leader, local, "the Raft leader is this node")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/keyspaces?type=user ([the case's
        // keyspace]), GET /storage_service/keyspaces (every keyspace, system
        // ones too), ?type=non_local_strategy (the five that are not
        // LocalStrategy), GET /column_family/name ("<keyspace>:<table>" for
        // every table), /column_family/name/keyspace (every keyspace again)
        // and /column_family/ (an object per table: ks, cf, type); the tapes
        // have these lists sorted, see "Order that is not deterministic".
        // Then GET /storage_service/natural_endpoints/
        // tcae_keyspaces?cf=items&key=1 (the replicas of a partition key: one
        // address) and GET /storage_service/ownership/tcae_keyspaces (the
        // fraction of the ring per address: "1", collapsed).
        spec.it("lists keyspaces and maps a key to its replica") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("lists_keyspaces_and_maps_a_key_to_its_replica", "tcae_keyspaces")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/storage_service/keyspaces?type=user", "[\"tcae_keyspaces\"]")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/keyspaces", "\"tcae_keyspaces\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/keyspaces?type=non_local_strategy", "\"tcae_keyspaces\"")
            expect_contains("/column_family/name", "\"tcae_keyspaces:items\"")
            expect_contains("/column_family/name/keyspace", "\"tcae_keyspaces\"")
            expect_contains("/column_family/", "\"cf\":\"items\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/natural_endpoints/tcae_keyspaces?cf=items&key=1", "[\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/ownership/tcae_keyspaces", "\"value\":\"")
            finish(rec, "tcae_keyspaces")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /column_family/metrics/<what>/tcae_metrics:items, where
        // a table is "<keyspace>:<table>": write (2 rows written), read (0),
        // live_ss_table_count (0, nothing flushed yet), pending_flushes,
        // pending_compactions, memtable_switch_count; each a bare number.
        // Then GET .../write/tcae_metrics:nope and GET .../write/nope:nope,
        // both 400 with "Can't find a column family".
        spec.it("reads the metrics of a table") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reads_the_metrics_of_a_table", "tcae_metrics")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/write/tcae_metrics:items", "2")
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/read/tcae_metrics:items", "0")
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/live_ss_table_count/tcae_metrics:items", "0")
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/pending_flushes/tcae_metrics:items", "0")
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/pending_compactions/tcae_metrics:items", "0")
            expect_body("/column_family/metrics/memtable_switch_count/tcae_metrics:items", "0")
            expect_error("GET", "/column_family/metrics/write/tcae_metrics:nope", 400, "Can't find a column family nope in keyspace tcae_metrics")
            expect_error("GET", "/column_family/metrics/write/nope:nope", 400, "Can't find a column family nope in keyspace nope")
            finish(rec, "tcae_metrics")
        }

        // PORTING: GET live_ss_table_count (0), POST /storage_service/
        // keyspace_flush/tcae_flush (200, empty body), GET live_ss_table_count
        // (1); then a cqlsh INSERT (not on the tape), POST keyspace_flush again,
        // GET live_ss_table_count (2); POST /storage_service/keyspace_compaction/
        // tcae_flush (200, empty body), GET live_ss_table_count (1). Then POST
        // /storage_service/keyspace_flush/nope: 400 "Can't find a keyspace nope".
        spec.it("flushes and compacts a keyspace") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("flushes_and_compacts_a_keyspace", "tcae_flush")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            count = "/column_family/metrics/live_ss_table_count/tcae_flush:items"
            expect_body(count, "0")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/keyspace_flush/tcae_flush")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "flush: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "", "an empty body")
            expect_body(count, "1")
            cql("INSERT INTO tcae_flush.items (id, name) VALUES (3, 'c')")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/keyspace_flush/tcae_flush")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "second flush: ${b}")
            expect_body(count, "2")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/keyspace_compaction/tcae_flush")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "compaction: ${b}")
            expect_body(count, "1")
            expect_error("POST", "/storage_service/keyspace_flush/nope", 400, "Can't find a keyspace nope")
            finish(rec, "tcae_flush")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/snapshots ([]), POST /storage_service/
        // snapshots?tag=tcae_snap&kn=tcae_snapshot (200, empty), GET
        // /storage_service/snapshots (one entry: {"key": tag, "value": [{"ks",
        // "cf", "total", "live"}]}, sizes collapsed to 0), DELETE
        // /storage_service/snapshots?tag=tcae_snap&kn=tcae_snapshot (200,
        // empty), GET /storage_service/snapshots ([] again). Then POST
        // .../snapshots?tag=x&kn=nope: 400 "Can't find a keyspace nope".
        spec.it("takes, lists and deletes a snapshot") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("takes_lists_and_deletes_a_snapshot", "tcae_snapshot")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/storage_service/snapshots", "[]")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/snapshots?tag=tcae_snap&kn=tcae_snapshot")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "snapshot: ${b}")
            st, b = rest("GET", "/storage_service/snapshots")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key\":\"tcae_snap\"", "the tag: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"ks\":\"tcae_snapshot\",\"cf\":\"items\"", "the table: ${b}")
            st, b = rest("DELETE", "/storage_service/snapshots?tag=tcae_snap&kn=tcae_snapshot")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete: ${b}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/snapshots", "[]")
            expect_error("POST", "/storage_service/snapshots?tag=x&kn=nope", 400, "Can't find a keyspace nope")
            finish(rec, "tcae_snapshot")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/schema_version (a UUID string), GET
        // /storage_proxy/schema_versions ([{"key": schema version, "value":
        // [address]}]: every node agrees on one), then a cqlsh CREATE TABLE
        // (not on the tape), then the same two GETs: the version is a different
        // UUID, {{uuid-N}} with a new N, and schema_versions agrees with it.
        spec.it("changes the schema version with a DDL statement") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("schema_version_changes_with_a_ddl_statement", "tcae_schema")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, v1 = rest("GET", "/storage_service/schema_version")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "schema_version: ${v1}")
            st, vs1 = rest("GET", "/storage_proxy/schema_versions")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "schema_versions: ${vs1}")
            spec.assert_contains(vs1, string.substring(v1, 1, string.length(v1) - 1), "one version, the node's own")
            cql("CREATE TABLE tcae_schema.more (id int PRIMARY KEY)")
            st, v2 = rest("GET", "/storage_service/schema_version")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "schema_version after: ${v2}")
            spec.assert_true(v1 != v2, "a DDL statement changes the schema version")
            st, vs2 = rest("GET", "/storage_proxy/schema_versions")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "schema_versions after: ${vs2}")
            spec.assert_contains(vs2, string.substring(v2, 1, string.length(v2) - 1), "and agreement on the new one")
            finish(rec, "tcae_schema")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /system/logger (every logger's name) and GET
        // /storage_service/logging_level ({"key": logger, "value": level} per
        // logger), both sorted on the tape (see "Order that is not
        // deterministic"); GET /system/logger/compaction ("info"), POST /system/logger/
        // compaction?level=debug (200, empty), GET (debug), POST ...?level=info,
        // GET (info). Errors: POST ...?level=loud is 400 "Unknown logging
        // level loud", GET /system/logger/nonexistent is 400 "Unknown logger
        // name nonexistent".
        spec.it("sets and resets a log level") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("sets_and_resets_a_log_level", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_contains("/system/logger", "\"compaction\"")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/logging_level", "\"compaction\"")
            expect_body("/system/logger/compaction", "\"info\"")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/system/logger/compaction?level=debug")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set debug: ${b}")
            expect_body("/system/logger/compaction", "\"debug\"")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/system/logger/compaction?level=info")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set info: ${b}")
            expect_body("/system/logger/compaction", "\"info\"")
            expect_error("POST", "/system/logger/compaction?level=loud", 400, "Unknown logging level loud")
            expect_error("GET", "/system/logger/nonexistent", 400, "Unknown logger name nonexistent")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_service/trace_probability (0), POST
        // .../trace_probability?probability=0.25, GET (0.25), POST
        // ...?probability=0 (back), GET (0). GET /storage_service/slow_query
        // ({"enable": false, "ttl": 86400, "threshold": 500000, "fast":
        // false}), POST /storage_service/slow_query?enable=true&threshold=1000,
        // GET (enable true, threshold 1000), POST ?enable=false&threshold=500000
        // (back), GET (as at first).
        spec.it("sets and resets tracing and slow query settings") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("sets_and_resets_tracing_and_slow_query_settings", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/storage_service/trace_probability", "0")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/trace_probability?probability=0.25")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set probability: ${b}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/trace_probability", "0.25")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/trace_probability?probability=0")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "reset probability: ${b}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/trace_probability", "0")
            slow = "{\"enable\":false,\"ttl\":86400,\"threshold\":500000,\"fast\":false}"
            expect_body("/storage_service/slow_query", slow)
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/slow_query?enable=true&threshold=1000")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "enable slow query: ${b}")
            expect_contains("/storage_service/slow_query", "\"enable\":true,\"ttl\":86400,\"threshold\":1000")
            st, b = rest("POST", "/storage_service/slow_query?enable=false&threshold=500000")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "reset slow query: ${b}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/slow_query", slow)
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /gossiper/endpoint/live ([address]), /gossiper/endpoint/
        // down ([]), /failure_detector/simple_states ([{"key": address,
        // "value": "UP"}]), /failure_detector/count/endpoint/up (1), .../down
        // (0), /failure_detector/phi (8, the convict threshold),
        // /failure_detector/endpoint_phi_values ([]: no peers to measure).
        spec.it("reports gossip and the failure detector") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_gossip_and_the_failure_detector", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, live = rest("GET", "/gossiper/endpoint/live")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "live: ${live}")
            spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(live, "[\"") == 1, "one address: ${live}")
            expect_body("/gossiper/endpoint/down", "[]")
            expect_contains("/failure_detector/simple_states", "\"value\":\"UP\"")
            expect_body("/failure_detector/count/endpoint/up", "1")
            expect_body("/failure_detector/count/endpoint/down", "0")
            expect_body("/failure_detector/phi", "8")
            expect_body("/failure_detector/endpoint_phi_values", "[]")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /storage_proxy/rpc_timeout (10), read_rpc_timeout (5),
        // write_rpc_timeout (2), range_rpc_timeout (10), truncate_rpc_timeout
        // (60), cas_contention_timeout (1), hinted_handoff_enabled (true),
        // hinted_handoff_enabled_by_dc ([]), read_repair_attempted (0). Then
        // the calls this Scylla answers 500 "API call is not supported yet":
        // GET /storage_proxy/max_hint_window, /storage_proxy/total_hints,
        // /hinted_handoff/hints, /storage_service/tombstone_warn_threshold.
        spec.it("reports storage proxy settings and unsupported calls") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_storage_proxy_settings_and_unsupported_calls", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/rpc_timeout", "10")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/read_rpc_timeout", "5")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/write_rpc_timeout", "2")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/range_rpc_timeout", "10")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/truncate_rpc_timeout", "60")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/cas_contention_timeout", "1")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/hinted_handoff_enabled", "true")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/hinted_handoff_enabled_by_dc", "[]")
            expect_body("/storage_proxy/read_repair_attempted", "0")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_proxy/max_hint_window", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_proxy/total_hints", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            expect_error("GET", "/hinted_handoff/hints", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/tombstone_warn_threshold", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /compaction_manager/compactions ([]: none running),
        // /compaction_manager/metrics/pending_tasks (0), GET /task_manager/
        // list_modules (the five task manager modules), /task_manager/ttl (0),
        // GET /stream_manager/ ([]), /storage_service/active_repair/ ([]),
        // /storage_service/raft_topology/upgrade ("done").
        spec.it("reports the compaction, task and stream managers") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_compaction_task_and_stream_managers", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/compaction_manager/compactions", "[]")
            expect_body("/compaction_manager/metrics/pending_tasks", "0")
            expect_body("/task_manager/list_modules", "[\"sstables_loader\",\"repair\",\"node_ops\",\"snapshot\",\"compaction\"]")
            expect_body("/task_manager/ttl", "0")
            expect_body("/stream_manager/", "[]")
            expect_body("/storage_service/active_repair/", "[]")
            expect_body("/storage_service/raft_topology/upgrade", "\"done\"")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /cache_service/row_cache_save_period, key_cache_save_period,
        // counter_cache_save_period (0 each), GET /cache_service/metrics/key/
        // capacity (0), /metrics/key/entries (0), /metrics/counter/capacity (0).
        // (/metrics/row/capacity, 484442112, is left out: a bare number of nine
        // digits would be collapsed like the uptime.) Then GET /cache_service/
        // row_cache_keys_to_save: 500 "API call is not supported yet".
        spec.it("reports the cache service") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_cache_service", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_body("/cache_service/row_cache_save_period", "0")
            expect_body("/cache_service/key_cache_save_period", "0")
            expect_body("/cache_service/counter_cache_save_period", "0")
            expect_body("/cache_service/metrics/key/capacity", "0")
            expect_body("/cache_service/metrics/key/entries", "0")
            expect_body("/cache_service/metrics/counter/capacity", "0")
            expect_error("GET", "/cache_service/row_cache_keys_to_save", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /system/uptime_ms (a bare number of milliseconds,
        // collapsed to 1000000), /storage_service/data_file/locations (["/var/
        // lib/scylla/data"]), /storage_service/saved_caches/location, /storage_
        // service/commitlog, /storage_service/incremental_backups (false),
        // /storage_service/compaction_throughput (0).
        spec.it("reports the uptime and the node's paths") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_uptime_and_the_nodes_paths", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, up = rest("GET", "/system/uptime_ms")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "uptime_ms: ${up}")
            expect_body("/storage_service/data_file/locations", "[\"/var/lib/scylla/data\"]")
            expect_body("/storage_service/saved_caches/location", "\"/var/lib/scylla/saved_caches\"")
            expect_body("/storage_service/commitlog", "\"/var/lib/scylla/commitlog\"")
            expect_body("/storage_service/incremental_backups", "false")
            expect_body("/storage_service/compaction_throughput", "0")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: GET /api-doc (the Swagger 1.2 index: {"apiVersion": "0.0.1",
        // "swaggerVersion": "1.2", "apis": [{"path": "/system", ...}, ...]}) and
        // GET /api-doc/system/ (the module's own description). The address in
        // the second's "basePath" is the replay server's own: {{request.host}}
        // on the tape, so a replay answers with the host:port it runs on.
        // (GET /api-doc/system, without the slash, is a 301 to the slash form.)
        spec.it("describes the API with swagger") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("describes_the_api_with_swagger", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_contains("/api-doc", "\"swaggerVersion\":\"1.2\"")
            expect_contains("/api-doc", "{\"path\":\"/storage_service\",\"description\":\"The storage service API\"}")
            expect_contains("/api-doc/system/", "\"resourcePath\":\"/system\"")
            finish(rec, "")
        }

        // PORTING: the representative errors. GET /nope and GET /storage_
        // service/nope: 404 {"message": "Not found", "code": 404}; GET
        // /messaging_service/version: 400 "Missing mandatory parameter 'addr'";
        // GET /storage_service/toppartitions/: 400 "Missing mandatory parameter
        // 'duration'"; GET /storage_service/repair_status/?id=1: 400 "unknown
        // repair id 1"; POST /storage_service/keyspace_compaction/nope: 400
        // "Can't find a keyspace nope"; GET /storage_service/describe_ring/nope:
        // 400 (a keyspace that is not there); GET /storage_service/stream_
        // throughput: 500 "API call is not supported yet".
        spec.it("answers errors with 400, 404 and 500") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_errors_with_400_404_and_500", "")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            expect_error("GET", "/nope", 404, "Not found")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/nope", 404, "Not found")
            expect_error("GET", "/messaging_service/version", 400, "Missing mandatory parameter 'addr'")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/toppartitions/", 400, "Missing mandatory parameter 'duration'")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/repair_status/?id=1", 400, "unknown repair id 1")
            expect_error("POST", "/storage_service/keyspace_compaction/nope", 400, "Can't find a keyspace nope")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/describe_ring/nope", 400, "nope")
            expect_error("GET", "/storage_service/stream_throughput", 500, "API call is not supported yet")
            finish(rec, "")
        }
    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("scylladb: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
